fn.p:
TP, TN, FP and FN represent the number of true positives, true negatives, false positives and false negatives, respectively. The Accuracy, Recall, Precision, F1-score and MCC are defined as follows: \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
\usepackage{amsmath}
\usepackage{wasysym}
\usepackage{amsfonts}
\usepackage{amssymb}
\usepackage{amsbsy}
\usepackage{upgreek}
\usepackage{mathrsfs}
\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
\begin{document}
$Accuracy = (TP + TN)/(TP + TN + FP + FN), Precision = TP/(TP+FP), Recall = TP/(TP+FN), F1-score = 2 \times Precision \times Recall/(Precision + Recall), MCC = (TP \times TN - FP \times FN) / \sqrt{(TP+FP)(TP+FN)(TN+FP)(TN+FN)}$\end{document}

